  "notes": "Technical report (arXiv 2503.19786), not a system card. Safety section (§6–7) is mostly qualitative. Figure 9 memorization bars are chart-only on a log scale with no numeric labels in the text layer; skipped evalResults rather than invent percentages (same approach as other Google TR extractions). Baseline assurance and CBRN give only qualitative claims (significantly low / low knowledge). FSF is cited without domain CCL outcomes, so riskDecisions empty. Child/self-harm appear only in the policy list, so those topics are covered false per pilot review rules. Hallucination appears only as post-training data filtering, not a behavior eval. Seed-linked google/gemma-3-270m-it is not named in this report (Gemma 3 here is 1B–27B only). Skipped all capability tables (Chatbot Arena Elo, MMLU, math/code/vision/multilingual/long-context, etc.). Two-column PDF hyphenates many quotes. FACTS Grounding rows from Table 6 (hallucination); SimpleQA skipped as capability."
